le we will use air in  many of the new technologies we  replenish water through water  replenishment projects capture rainwater  give back and then we recycle the water  and give back to the municipalities as  clean water to those are the three ways  and we have reduced our water by twenty  percent over the last five years we will  reduce our water further twenty plus  percent in the next four years and we  will become watering  through by 2020 water is also  fundamental to women's economic  empowerment as I mentioned before just  one simple link in terms of how you  emancipate women in Africa through  bringing water and how you can then  start empowering them so this sort of  brings us full cycle smart organizations  I think those that succeed over the next  decade and beyond will understand that  the 21st century is the women's century  women's economic empowerment and  entrepreneurial growth will drive I  believe the world's economy it's not a  matter of if but a matter of 21 height  not a matter of if so for all of us in  business education government civil  society the implications I think are  going to be very vast very profound I  think everyone's success I believe is  going to be contingent upon woman's  success and we think that way and unless  you think that way I don't think you can  do justice to the opportunity so and and  again let me be clear this is not a  battle of the sexes it is not far from  it this is actually a battle for  preserving and enhancing the world's  economic environmental and social fabric  so it's that simple no one knows this I  think more what I just said then all of  you here at Yale which I think has  flourished to an incredible level of  height since you have gone  co-educational 40 years ago and I  therefore wish you all the best of  success in your future role in ensuring  that the 21st century will be the  women's  so thank you for giving me this  opportunity all of you and it's been a  great pleasure and honor to be here  t